chore: rename branch to main and add publishing guide

The app fetches providers from
raw.githubusercontent.com/<author>/vega-providers/<branch>/manifest.json
and its default branch constant is "main". This repo was on "master",
which would 404 after publishing.

PUBLISH.md walks through creating the repo, pushing, installing in the app,
and the common failure modes (wrong repo name, private repo, stale raw
cache, forgetting to rebuild dist/).

Pre-publish checks all pass: manifest lists 8 providers, each has its 4
modules in dist/, no orphan dist directories, all 32 modules load under
Node, and a fresh build produces no diff.
